{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "11d21b6c-fe50-5d04-8a57-b888f5b276e1",
  "Description": "World gravity is off; a radial force pulls 200 moons onto a planet.\n\n[RigidForce] in Radial mode replaces gravity with a pull towards one point. The moons are one [RigidBody] with a point per body from [ScatterPointsInVolume], and a shared LinearVelocity gives them a sideways drift.\n\nAKA: gravity, attractor, orbit, radial force, planet\n\nTips\n- A negative Strength pushes the moons away instead.\n- Radius and Falloff limit how far the pull reaches.",
